.TH KONGFIG 1 "2026-10-13" "kongfig" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kongfig \- manage simple configuration values via symbolic links
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kongfig
.RI [ \-\-folder ]
.br
.B kongfig
.RI [ \-\-folder ]
.I key
.br
.B kongfig
.RI [ \-\-folder ]
.I key
.I value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kongfig
stores configuration entries as symbolic links in a directory tree.

By default, the storage directory is:
.IP
.B $HOME/.config/kongfig

If the environment variable
.B KONGFIG
is set, that path is used instead.

A parameter that begins with
.B \-\-
names a subfolder of that directory. The leading dashes are not part of
the folder name. It may appear in any position; the remaining parameters
are the key and optional value.

The command supports three forms:
.TP
.B kongfig
.RI [ \-\-folder ]
List entries in the configured directory, or in
.I folder
when given (if it exists).
.TP
.B kongfig
.RI [ \-\-folder ]
.I key
Show a single entry for
.IR key .
If the key exists and is a symbolic link, the command prints link details.
.TP
.B kongfig
.RI [ \-\-folder ]
.I key value
Create or replace
.I key
so it points to
.IR value .
With
.BR \-\-folder ,
the link is created at
.IR $KONGFIG/folder/key .

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I \-\-folder
Subfolder of the storage directory. The name after the leading dashes
must not contain
.BR / ,
and must not be
.B .
or
.BR .. .
.TP
.I key
Configuration key name. The key must not contain the slash character
.RB ( / ).
.TP
.I value
Configuration value. Values are stored as symlink targets and may contain
.RB ( / ),
so a target may be a filesystem path.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KONGFIG
Root directory used by the command.
Default: 
.BR $HOME/.config/kongfig .

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid input (for example, a key or subfolder contains a slash,
or more than one subfolder is given).

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
KONGFIG=/tmp/kfg kongfig name "Fred Flintstone"
KONGFIG=/tmp/kfg kongfig name
KONGFIG=/tmp/kfg kongfig
KONGFIG=/tmp/kfg kongfig --xyz a b
.fi
.PP
The last example stores
.I b
at
.BR /tmp/kfg/xyz/a .

.SH NOTES
.IP \[bu] 2
The current script prints the selected storage directory as
.B KONGFIG=<path>
on each run.
.IP \[bu] 2
The command does not support option flags such as
.B -k
or
.BR -v .
A parameter beginning with
.B \-\-
names a subfolder, not an option.
Those flags belong to the separate
.B kongfigtest
program in this repository.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kongfigtest (1),
.BR ln (1),
.BR readlink (1)
